1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=vwLc5RCG78cQ7kNvwHRsgni&_nc_oc=AdqsW604lK407e_TGigwUVm6G68aLRhQctmr8BX5wmkMp9CfF2h3BHRxW3EVnyNZhJY&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f30f&oh=00_AQVuHY3NqduWM9rIYddO4IeF1_XMx3onuwSjvdG-ZRhHGw&oe=6B0EF8D3"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "DUET Solar System 360", "keywords": ["space", "astronomy", "planets", "education", "science"], "long_description": "DUET Solar System 360 shows school students what space is really like, with real distances, real textures and real missions.\n\n- VR deep space: float inside a life-size Solar System and fly between the Sun, the planets and their moons.\n- Mixed reality: see your own room with the Solar System floating in it, and walk around it.\n- Every planet and major moon in 3D with NASA surface maps, with facts on size, distance, gravity, day length and temperature.\n- 16 real spacecraft in 3D, including Voyager, Hubble, the James Webb telescope, the ISS, Cassini, Juno and the Mars rovers.\n- The Milky Way and the night sky from NASA's 8K star map, with constellations and nearby stars.\n- Moon landings, including Chandrayaan-3 at the lunar south pole.\n- 177 photographs from real missions.\n- Orbits that can be switched on or off, and adjustable speed.\n- Works offline after the first launch.\n\nFor schools: full access comes with a DUET STEM school subscription code. Without a code, a free 10-minute demo is available every day.", "short_description": "Stand inside a life-size Solar System: fly between the Sun, planets and moons, see real spacecraft up close, and bring the planets into your own room in mixed reality."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://ashutoshduet.github.io/duet-lms-media/space/privacy.html", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "DUET Power", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://ashutoshduet.github.io/duet-lms-media/space/", "category": null, "comfort_rati